{{Character
|Trainer Class=Goth
|Main Details=Boss of [[Greenwash HQ]].

== Speech Style ==
Dismissive: Rejects ethical concerns and risks as insignificant (''"a few casualties are a small price to pay," "You're just a pessimist"'')

Profit-Driven: Quickly pivots noble scientific discoveries into lucrative ventures (charging a premium for de-fossilating creatures).

Propagandist: In emails, he uses reassuring language to maintain control and morale, demanding staff ''"disregard any rumors"'' while acknowledging previous failures.

Hubristic: Believes he has the power to ''"create life"'' and ''"shape the future"'' by playing God.

== Tone ==
Ambitious, Unethical, and Authoritarian. Focused relentlessly on ''scientific advancement'' and ''potential profits,'' dismissing ethical and safety concerns as ''pessimism.'' When a project fails, his tone shifts to denial and urgency (''"Shut it down now!"'')

== Focus ==
Driving controversial research forward at any cost. He prioritizes Omnichannel’s goals and suppresses dissent to maintain momentum, regardless of consequences.

== Role & Actions ==
The driving force behind two major projects: the De-Fossilator and the Fusion Experiment. Uses his authority to override objections from colleagues like Dempsey and Selby, forcing continuation of dangerous, Omnichannel-backed research.

== Key Projects & Conflicts ==
* '''De-Fossilator''': Co-developed with Selby, driven by profit over scientific good.
* '''Fusion Experiment''': Desperate to produce breakthroughs for Omnichannel; responsible for unstable and dangerous creations (e.g., Ant/Aardorn fusion).
* '''Internal Conflict''': Frequently clashes with Dempsey and Chip over ethical and safety concerns.
}}